Introduction
Within ASML, the Machine Conditioning (MC) department is responsible for conditioning our lithography machines. Our objective is to precisely control the temperature of the critical areas in the machine and to keep products clean of particle and chemical contamination. Besides this we control the vacuum in our EUV tool, which is also a part of our responsibility. This is accomplished by systems with controlled water cooling and controlled ultra-high purity gas flows. You work with temperature control and gas conditioning, which is essential in reducing the environmental footprint of our machines – an essential part of our sustainability goals.
Your Assignment
As an intern in our team, you will work on an interesting assignment that deals with gas and water manifolds, piping, sensors and vacuum feedthroughs.
Some of your tasks will include:
Identify cost drivers in the existing design(s);
Gather input from internal experts and external suppliers;
Propose design changes and review them with appropriate stakeholders;
Document and present your proposals;
Implement the proposed design changes.
This is a Bachelor/Master apprentice internship (non-thesis) for a duration of 5-6 months working 4-5 days per week (3 days onsite). The start date of this internship is as soon as possible, or the latest around September.
Your Profile
To be a fit for this assignment, you:
Are busy with your bachelor's or master's in Engineering (Mechanical, Aerospace, Industrial, etc.);
Are proactive and result-oriented;
Are interested in working in a technical environment;
Have good communication skills in English (verbal and written).
