Introduction
The goal of your project is to increase the speed of the EUV machine in terms of wafers per hour (throughput), which increases value of EUV lithography machines to customers and help resolve the global electronics shortage in the next generation product development. To maximize the throughput the system needs to have a very high availability (>95%) and thus needs to have a high reliability.
One of the challenges is to test both the functionality as well as the reliability both thorough as well as fast. As the machine grows the modules also become more complex and the need for quality increases further. To minimize time and cost tests are executed at various levels, from simulations to full system tests.
Your Assignment
With the aid of experienced integrator and other engineering disciplines, you will continue previous work done on the validation and improvements of the existing test framework. This includes work on test benches, python coding, usage of various automated test equipment like scopes, waveform generators, Data packet sniffer tool etc.
Your tasks will include:
(Statistical) Analysis of test results. Understand firmware/HSI modifications and make it possible to test;
Modify and extend the python test framework. Determining suitable roadmap for the test framework;
Come up with a verification approach of the testbench;
Oversee the test setup and methodology and propose improvements;
Test and validate written scripts;
Improve automated interaction with test tooling;
Create test dashboarding;
This is a bachelor/master apprentice internship (to gain work experience) or a bachelor thesis for a duration of 3-9 months months. The start date is in September 2025.
Your Profile
To be a perfect fit for this assignment, you:
​Have a background in Electrical Engineering, Software Engineering or related;
Have knowledge of programming (python), statistical analysis and communication interfaces.;
Are capable and interested to do hands on work, interpreting data and prove hypothesis;
Have an interest in electronics, measurement equipment, test automation and software;
Are capable of explaining the technical details to someone unfamiliar with this technology, as you will be working within a multidisciplinary team.
